1
00:00:01,319 --> 00:00:06,160
But they woke at dawn, as usual, and suddenly remembering the glorious thing

2
00:00:06,160 --> 00:00:10,759
that had happened, they all raced out into the pasture together.

3
00:00:10,759 --> 00:00:15,640
A little way down the pasture, there was a knoll that commanded a view of most of

4
00:00:15,640 --> 00:00:17,079
the farm.

5
00:00:17,079 --> 00:00:23,920
The animals rushed to the top of it and gazed round them in the clear morning light.

6
00:00:23,920 --> 00:00:26,559
Yes, it was theirs.

7
00:00:26,559 --> 00:00:30,440
Everything that they could see was theirs.

8
00:00:30,440 --> 00:00:35,440
In the ecstasy of that thought, they gamboled round and round. They hurled

9
00:00:35,440 --> 00:00:41,119
themselves into the air in great leaps of excitement. They rolled in the dew.

10
00:00:41,119 --> 00:00:45,960
They cropped mouthfuls of the sweet summer grass. They kicked up clods of

11
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:50,359
the black earth and snuffed its rich scent.

12
00:00:50,359 --> 00:00:55,000
Then they made a tour of inspection of the whole farm and surveyed, with

13
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:03,559
speechless admiration, the plowland, the hayfield, the orchard, the pool, the spinney.

14
00:01:03,559 --> 00:01:08,160
It was as though they had never seen these things before, and even now they

15
00:01:08,160 --> 00:01:11,960
could hardly believe that it was all their own.

16
00:01:11,960 --> 00:01:15,960
Then they filed back to the farm buildings and halted in silence outside

17
00:01:15,960 --> 00:01:18,119
the door of the farmhouse.

18
00:01:18,119 --> 00:01:23,480
That was theirs, too, but they were frightened to go inside.

19
00:01:23,480 --> 00:01:28,079
After a moment, however, Snowball and Napoleon butted the door open with their

20
00:01:28,079 --> 00:01:32,920
shoulders, and the animals entered in single file, walking with the utmost

21
00:01:32,920 --> 00:01:36,039
care for fear of disturbing anything.

22
00:01:36,039 --> 00:01:41,359
They tiptoed from room to room, afraid to speak above a whisper,

23
00:01:41,359 --> 00:01:48,000
and gazing with a kind of awe at the unbelievable luxury, at the beds with their feather

24
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:54,079
mattresses, the looking glasses, the horsehair sofa, the Brussels carpet, the

25
00:01:54,079 --> 00:01:58,640
lithograph of Queen Victoria over the drawing-room mantelpiece.

26
00:01:58,640 --> 00:02:02,680
They were just coming down the stairs when Molly was discovered to be missing.

27
00:02:02,680 --> 00:02:07,799
Going back, the others found that she had remained behind in the best bedroom.

28
00:02:07,799 --> 00:02:12,119
She had taken a piece of blue ribbon from Mrs. Jones's dressing table and was

29
00:02:12,119 --> 00:02:18,680
holding it against her shoulder and admiring herself in the glass in a very foolish manner.

30
00:02:18,680 --> 00:02:22,599
The others reproached her sharply, and they went outside.

31
00:02:22,599 --> 00:02:26,799
Some hams hanging in the kitchen were taken out for burial, and the barrel of

32
00:02:26,799 --> 00:02:30,759
beer in the scullery was stove in with a kick from Boxer's hoof.

33
00:02:30,759 --> 00:02:33,960
Otherwise, nothing in the house was touched.

34
00:02:33,960 --> 00:02:38,000
A unanimous resolution was passed on the spot that the farmhouse should be

35
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,240
preserved as a museum.

36
00:02:40,240 --> 00:02:44,000
All were agreed that no animal must ever live there.
